UX_DEVICE_CLASS_CDC_ACM_ZERO_COPY|UX_DEVICE_CLASS_CDC_ACM_ZERO_COPY|Device Class CDC ACM||||Defined, it enables device CDC ACM zero copy for bulk in/out endpoints (write/read). Enabled, the endpoint buffer is not allocated in class, application must provide the buffer for read/write, and the buffer must meet device controller driver (DCD) buffer requirements (e.g., aligned and cache safe). It only works if UX_DEVICE_ENDPOINT_BUFFER_OWNER is 1 (endpoint buffer managed by class).
