UX_DEVICE_ENDPOINT_BUFFER_OWNER|UX_DEVICE_ENDPOINT_BUFFER_OWNER|Device Core||||Defined, this value represents the endpoint buffer owner. 0 - The default, endpoint buffer is managed by core stack. Each endpoint takes UX_SLAVE_REQUEST_DATA_MAX_LENGTH bytes. 1 - Endpoint buffer managed by classes. In this case not all endpoints consume UX_SLAVE_REQUEST_DATA_MAX_LENGTH bytes.
UX_DEVICE_ENABLE_GET_STRING_WITH_ZERO_LANGUAGE_ID|UX_DEVICE_ENABLE_GET_STRING_WITH_ZERO_LANGUAGE_ID|Device Core||||Defined, this enables processing of Get String Descriptor requests with zero Language ID. The first language ID in the language ID framework will be used if the request has a zero Language ID.
