UX_DEVICE_CLASS_PRINTER_ZERO_COPY|UX_DEVICE_CLASS_PRINTER_ZERO_COPY|Device Class Printer||||Defined, it enables zero copy support (works if PRINTER owns endpoint buffer). Defined, it enables zero copy for bulk in/out endpoints (write/read). In this case, the endpoint buffer is not allocated in class, application must provide the buffer for read/write, and the buffer must meet device controller driver (DCD) buffer requirements (e.g., aligned and cache safe if buffer is for DMA).
